# GitHub's language bar measures bytes, and ~89% of a rendered notebook's bytes
# are base64-encoded chart images from its saved outputs. That skewed the repo to
# "86% Jupyter Notebook" and buried the actual application code at 3% Python.
# Marking notebooks as documentation excludes them from the language statistics
# while keeping them fully rendered and browsable on GitHub.
*.ipynb linguist-documentation

# Reference papers, not source.
project/documents/** linguist-documentation
